    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d725">

                <pb facs="0864" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.70/11–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-08T15:00:00-04:00">November 8, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9345. For EITO Delegation. ReEmbs 9364, October 30, 1944. Department agrees that
                    if during the period of US participation in EITO present controls are liquidated
                    or materially altered it might be impossible for this Government to honor fully
                    its commitments under Article VIII, section 4 as presently drafted.</p>
                <p>The text in the immediately following clear telegram has been approved by the
                    interested divisions of ECA<anchor n="74" xml:id="d725-f1"/> and WEA<anchor
                        n="75" xml:id="d725-f2"/> and is <pb facs="0865" n="855" xml:id="pg855"/>
                    submitted as a possible substitute. It has not been submitted to the Postwar
                    Program Committee. Your comments are solicited. This new text might also be more
                    acceptable to the British and the continental powers since they too may lack
                    adequate controls to implement this section as originally drafted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
